⚠⚠⚠ AND ONE ROW WAS RECORDED AS UNRESOLVED RATHER THAN AS A VERDICT: S3a.
Measured under gNoUnwrap ON, `**x` on a ONE-deep pointer READ THE LEAF where the
law says the second star must refuse. That is the signature of a fixpoint. But
the reading CANNOT BE TRUSTED YET, because both available witnesses are
compromised:
  - printing a pointer FOLLOWS THE CHAIN, so a value witness cannot tell "read
    one level" from "read to the leaf";
  - the identity witness -- passing the result to an action and printing
    `argument.taG` -- returns `argument`, because reading a tag through an
    action-argument holder yields the HOLDER. That is the carrier defect this
    campaign exists to fix (incant/holderT row 3).
SO THE INSTRUMENT NEEDED TO CERTIFY THE STAR LAW IS BLOCKED BY THE DEFECT THE
CAMPAIGN IS FIXING, and S3a is reported as unmeasured rather than graded. Do not
read its flip-OFF green as evidence about the law -- flip-OFF it refuses for the
auto-unwrap's reasons, not the law's.
⚠ WHEN THE CARRIER LANDS, S3a GETS ITS IDENTITY WITNESS AND BECOMES THE ROW THIS
FILE WAS BUILT FOR. Until then S4 is the only row asserting something the law
uniquely predicts.

HOW TO READ THE ROWS.

S1 and S2a are the same shape at different depths and are the positive controls:
a single star takes exactly one level off, so on a one-deep pointer it reaches
the leaf and on a two-deep pointer it reaches the middle.

S2b and S3b are composition: two stars off a two-deep pointer, three off a
three-deep, both reaching the leaf. If `*` were still overshooting by one -- the
pre-SEQ-111 behaviour -- these would refuse instead.

S3a IS THE CERTIFICATE. Two stars on a ONE-deep pointer is one star too many, so
the second star is past the leaf and must refuse. Under the retired `**`
fixpoint operator this row READ THE LEAF, because a fixpoint stops when it stops
rather than counting. A green S3a is the only thing standing between the law and
a silent return of the fixpoint.

S4 IS THE ANTI-VACUITY CONTROL AND IS RE-READ ON EVERY RUN. A star on a bare
leaf must refuse by name. If it ever succeeds, every refusal row above becomes
unfalsifiable -- there would be nothing left that a star cannot read -- so S4 is
what makes S3a mean anything.
